the target language is: prolog.

the knowledge base termlife_grace_check includes these resources:
    temporal.

the functions are:
    the effective date of *an activity* is *a date*.
    the paid to date of the policy before *an activity* is *a date*.
    the policy status of the policy before *an activity* is *a value*.
    the days past due of *an activity* is *a number*.
    the in grace of *an activity* is *a value*.
    the grace period days of the plan is *a number*.

the templates are:
    *an activity* is a grace check.
    *an activity* spawns *a transaction*.

the knowledge base termlife_grace_check includes:

the text of "GraceCheck/Transaction.xml" is at "sources/GraceCheck/Transaction.xml".

the grace period days of the plan is 31, as stated in "PlanFields.csv" at GracePeriodDays.

% An activity of this program is a grace check: the GraceCheck transaction it processes.
an activity is a grace check if
    the effective date of the activity is a date.

rule days_past_due with provenance "GraceCheck/Transaction.xml" at MathVariable DaysPastDueMV:
the days past due of an activity is a number if
    the effective date of the activity is a date
    and the date is the number days after the paid to date of the policy before the activity.

rule in_grace with provenance "GraceCheck/Transaction.xml" at MathVariable InGraceMV:
the in grace of an activity is a value if
    the days past due of the activity is a number N
    and the grace period days of the plan is a number M
    and N > 0
        and N <= M
    and the value is equal to "Yes"
    otherwise the activity is a grace check
    and the value is equal to "No".

rule spawn_1 with provenance "GraceCheck/SpawnActivities.xml" at Spawn 1:
an activity spawns Lapse if
    the policy status of the policy before the activity is a value
    and the days past due of the activity > the grace period days of the plan
        and the value is equal to Active.

scenario monthly_payer_g1 is:
    the effective date of g1 is 2024-05-20.
    the paid to date of the policy before g1 is 2024-06-01.
    the policy status of the policy before g1 is Active.
    days_past_due expects answers ["the days past due of g1 is -12"].
    in_grace expects answers ["the in grace of g1 is No"].
    spawns expects answers [].

scenario monthly_payer_g2 is:
    the effective date of g2 is 2024-07-15.
    the paid to date of the policy before g2 is 2024-06-01.
    the policy status of the policy before g2 is Active.
    days_past_due expects answers ["the days past due of g2 is 44"].
    in_grace expects answers ["the in grace of g2 is No"].
    spawns expects answers ["g2 spawns Lapse"].

query days_past_due is:
    the days past due of which activity is which number.

query in_grace is:
    the in grace of which activity is which value.

query spawns is:
    which activity spawns which transaction.

the view grace_check is:
    the title is "GraceCheck (termlife)".
    the case is a scenario.
    the facts about "the activity" are
        the effective date of an activity is a date.
    the facts about "the policy it finds" are
        the paid to date of the policy before an activity is a date,
        the policy status of the policy before an activity is a value.
    the result is the answer to query days_past_due.
    the result shows its citations.

